IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa10-types.l4: the nouns that more than one of part coa10's modules (ss 441-474 of the Companies Act 2006) share.
-- DECLARE only: no rules, no #EVAL, no #ASSERT.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the official
-- text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
-- TARGET. The stable binary (main 1.6.110). No section GIVEN, no REFUSE, no sets, no TYPICALLY, no YMD.
--
-- Every name begins with the label of the provision that introduces it (the keel's naming rule).

-- THE TWO TEXTS. The text file prints two texts of s 444 (lines 5949-5982 and 5983-5993), of s 445(7) (lines 6019-6021
-- and 6022-6024), of s 446(5) (lines 6039-6042 and 6043-6046) and of the daily default fine in s 451(4) (line 6128, run
-- together). The file's own caveat (SOURCES.md, text_caveat) is that it "may carry more than one extent version of a
-- provision, and prospective provisions, which CLML marks but this text does not distinguish". The text does not say which
-- is in force, so the choice is an INPUT of every rule that depends on it, never merged (fork F1 in NOTES.md).
DECLARE `s 441 text of the sections the file prints twice` IS ONE OF
    `s 441 first text in the file`
    `s 441 second text in the file`

-- The documents the filing sections name.
-- src:5898 | (1) The directors of a company must deliver to the registrar for each financial year the accounts and reports required by—
-- src:5899 | section 443A (filing obligations of micro-entities),
-- src:5900 | section 444 (filing obligations of companies subject to small companies regime small companies other than micro-entities),
-- src:5901 | section 444A (filing obligations of companies entitled to small companies exemption in relation to directors' report),
-- src:5902 | section 445 (filing obligations of medium-sized companies),
-- src:5903 | section 446 (filing obligations of unquoted companies), or
-- src:5904 | section 447 (filing obligations of quoted companies).
@ref s 441(1) Duty to file accounts and reports with the registrar (src:5898-5904)
DECLARE `s 441 document` IS ONE OF
    `s 441 annual accounts`
    `s 441 balance sheet`
    `s 441 profit and loss account`
    `s 441 directors' report`
    `s 441 strategic report`
    `s 441 directors' remuneration report`
    `s 441 separate corporate governance statement`
    `s 441 auditor's report`
    `s 441 statement that all the members have consented to the abridgement`

-- What a filing section says about a document: a duty, a permission, or (where the text says so) no duty.
-- "Not covered" is NOTHING, outside this type.
DECLARE `s 441 requirement` IS ONE OF
    `s 441 the directors must deliver it`
    `s 441 the directors may deliver it`
    `s 441 the section does not require it`

-- The six sections of Chapter 10 that say which accounts and reports are required (s 441(1)).
DECLARE `s 441 filing section` IS ONE OF
    `s 441 section 443A`
    `s 441 section 444`
    `s 441 section 444A`
    `s 441 section 445`
    `s 441 section 446`
    `s 441 section 447`
